{
  "text": "On the authority of Abu Dhah, Jundub ibn Junadah, and Abu Abdur Rahman Mu'addah ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased of them both, that the Messenger of Allah, may the blessings and peace of Allah be upon him, said, Fear Allah wherever you are, and follow up a bad deed with a good one, and it will wipe it out, and behave well towards people. It was related by At-Tamidhi, who said it was a good hadith, and in some copies of At-Tamidhi's collection, it was said to be a good and sound hadith.",
